    "sha": "2649bb17ee8a7c1b5713bed64a1f077af2fc5b49",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDI2NDliYjE3ZWU4YTdjMWI1NzEzYmVkNjRhMWYwNzdhZjJmYzViNDk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-21T13:29:26Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-21T13:29:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(import): state the STEP length unit, and ask for it when the file has none\n\nA STEP model import now ends its notes with the length unit that the\nmodel was read in: the file's own, or the unit that the caller stated.\nA STEP file whose unit contexts state no length unit is no longer read\nas millimetres. It is refused with ImportError::StepUnitsMissing until\nthe caller states mm or in:\n\n- ImportModel::within_in / from_bytes_in, MCP import_model `units`,\n  and the fourth argument of cam.import;\n- the desktop app asks with a Length unit prompt (Millimeters, Inches,\n  Cancel) and runs the same import again in the answer, as one\n  undoable import. Cancel imports nothing.\n\nThe kernel writes the stated unit into the file's representation\ncontexts before the read (step_assumed_unit), so the tolerance, the\nedge-gap cap and the chord stay in the unit of the geometry. A file\nthat states its own unit keeps it; the note names a caller's unit that\nis not used. A unit for a mesh file is refused by name.\n\nFixes #1874\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
